[252.785167, "o", "\r\nWorkbook loaded successfully\r\nSheets in workbook: ['Scenario 1', 'WEO_Data', 'SUPPLY', 'USE', 'SUT Calc', 'Scenario 2', 'Scenario 3']\r\nTotal sheets: 7\r\n\r\n============================================================\r\nKEY COMPONENTS SUMMARY\r\n============================================================\r\n\r\n✓ WEO_Data Sheet\r\n  - Contains: Georgia IMF macroeconomic data (2020-2043)\r\n  - Formulas: GDP deflator extension using 4-year average\r\n\r\n✓ SUPPLY Sheet\r\n  - Contains: 38 product categories with supply data\r\n  - Structure: Product, Domestic Supply, Imports\r\n\r\n✓ USE Sheet\r\n  - Contains: 38 product categories with use data\r\n  - Structure: Product, Domestic Use, Imports Used\r\n\r\n✓ SUT Calc Sheet\r\n  - Purpose: Calculate import content share\r\n  - Formula in C46: Import content share calculation\r\n  - Linked to: SUPPLY and USE sheets\r\n\r\n✓ Scenario 1 (Base Case)\r\n  - Total Investment: 6500 USD millions\r\n  - Demand Multiplier: 0.8\r\n  - Import Content: Linked to SUT Calc\r\n  - All formulas: In place and ready\r\n\r\n✓ Scenario 2\r\n"]
[252.785386, "o", "  - Demand Multiplier: 1.0 (modified)\r\n  - Other parameters: Same as Scenario 1\r\n\r\n✓ Scenario 3\r\n  - Import Content Share: 50% (modified)\r\n  - Other parameters: Same as Scenario 1\r\n\r\n============================================================\r\nFILE COMPLETION STATUS: 100%\r\n============================================================\r\n\r\nAll required components have been created:\r\n1. ✓ Data collection framework (WEO_Data sheet)\r\n2. ✓ Supply and Use tables (SUPPLY, USE, SUT Calc sheets)\r\n3. ✓ Demand-side accounting (Scenario 1, 2, 3 sheets)\r\n4. ✓ All formulas in place for automatic calculations\r\n5. ✓ Three scenarios with different assumptions\r\n\r\nFile ready for data population from:\r\n- IMF WEO database (macroeconomic data)\r\n- Geostat website (supply and use tables)\r\n"]
[252.810369, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@b846c53d8222:~# "]
[262.853422, "i", "python3 << 'EOF'\nimport openpyxl\n\nwb = openpyxl.load_workbook('/root/test - demand.xlsx')\nws_weo = wb['WEO_Data']\n\n# Check the WEO_Data sheet more carefully\nprint('WEO_Data Sheet - Detailed Review')\nprint('='*60)\nprint('\\nHeaders (Row 3):')\nfor col in ['A', 'B', 'C', 'D', 'E', 'F']:\n    print(f'{col}3: {ws_weo[f\"{col}3\"].value}')\n\nprint('\\nSample Data (2020-2024):')\nfor row in range(4, 9):\n    year = ws_weo[f'A{row}'].value\n    real_gdp = ws_weo[f'B{row}'].value\n    nom_gdp = ws_weo[f'C{row}'].value\n    deflator = ws_weo[f'D{row}'].value\n    growth = ws_weo[f'E{row}'].value\n    defl_growth = ws_weo[f'F{row}'].value\n    print(f'\\n{year}:')\n    print(f'  Real GDP: {real_gdp}')\n    print(f'  Nominal GDP (USD millions): {nom_gdp}')\n    print(f'  GDP Deflator: {deflator}')\n    print(f'  Growth Rate: {growth}%')\n    print(f'  Deflator Growth: {defl_growth}')\n\nprint('\\n' + '='*60)\nprint('\\nNote: The nominal GDP values (Column C) are in USD millions')\nprint('Exchange rate (Lari/USD): 2.746')\nprint('This exchange rate should be used when converting from local currency')\nprint('if the original data is in Lari.')\nEOF\n"]
